	Abstract = {Lewis and Mordecki have computed the Wiener-Hopf factorization of a L$\backslash$'evy process whose restriction on \$]0,+\backslash infty[\$ of their L$\backslash$'evy measure has a rational Laplace transform. That allows to compute the distribution of \$(X\_t,\backslash inf\_\{0\backslash leq s\backslash leq t\}X\_s)\$. For the same class of L$\backslash$'evy processes, we compute the distribution of \$ (X\_t,\backslash inf\_\{0\backslash leq s\backslash leq t\}X\_s,\backslash sup\_\{0\backslash leq s\backslash leq t\} X\_s)\$ and also the behavior of this triple at certain stopping time, like the first exit time of an interval containing the origin. Some applications to the pricing of double barrier options with or without rebate are evocated.},
